@attribute [CmsBlockType(
    "rawHtml",
    "Raw HTML",
    Description = "A single block of HTML, sanitized on save and again on render.",
    IconKey = "bi-code",
    SummaryTemplate = "{content}")]
@inherits CmsBlockBase
@* The one property goes through CmsBlockProperty rather than being interpolated here, and for this
   block type that is load-bearing rather than stylistic: RawHtmlRenderer re-runs the sanitizer on
   the way out (ADR-0008), and markup that emitted the stored string itself would put whatever is in
   the database straight onto the page.

   No wrapper element beyond the marker div. A footer authored as raw HTML brings its own structure,
   and a <section> around it would put a landmark into every page that shows it. *@
<div class="cms-block cms-raw-html" data-block-type="rawHtml" data-block="@BlockId">
    <CmsBlockProperty Name="content" />
</div>
